/Title (Air is the most immediate human necessity, yet the way we understand its quality remains limited. While air pollution is a major public health concern in India, most systems today only present Air Quality Index \(AQI\) values without meaningful interpretation. These numbers fail to communicate real-world impact, leaving citizens and decision-makers without clarity on causes, risks, or actions. This disconnect between data and understanding creates a critical need for systems that can translate air quality data into actionable intelligence.)
